<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Zarumilla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecuadorian-peruvian-war">Ecuadorian–Peruvian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Zarumilla was fought in July 1941 near the Zarumilla River on the border between Ecuador and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. A larger, better-equipped Peruvian army, using aircraft and paratroops, defeated the Ecuadorian forces and occupied the province of El Oro. The defeat forced Ecuador to accept the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-protocol">Rio de Janeiro Protocol</a> of 1942, which gave most of the disputed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amazon">Amazon</a> territory to Peru.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-zarumilla.jpg" alt="Battle of Zarumilla" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SuperMundo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ecuador_en_guerra.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
